{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3898","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3898","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3898\",\"parent_revision\":\"b2f81e9b4f98dc5aed31fe9b21a705ae80e1f822ec33bfd0b6ed15d79c952e60\",\"root_revision\":\"b2f81e9b4f98dc5aed31fe9b21a705ae80e1f822ec33bfd0b6ed15d79c952e60\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Requested Outcome\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAddress the investigation-guidance gaps identified while discussing failing CI. The process must determine whether the product, its architecture, the test oracle, or the test/CI harness needs correction; green CI alone is not the decision criterion.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Baseline\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nInspected main: `9dc96e51be1f277345207c8d9664c17ecda2b095`.\\n\\n- DH and Python `test-failure-mindset`, plus `python3-testing`, present tests as authoritative specifications before considering incorrect expectations.\\n- DH `root-cause-tracing-process` distinguishes runtime evidence poorly from requirement authority and its non-reproducible branch requires deterministic all-or-none results.\\n- DH and Python `comprehensive-test-review` lead with generic coverage percentages rather than evidence of contract validity and fault detection. Python's shared standards already say not to invent universal coverage targets.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Change Contract And Plan\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Preserve the evidence-chain, safe reproduction, source citation, uncertainty, and no-symptom-patching safeguards.\\n2. Treat tests as claims to validate against authoritative intent; trace both product execution and test observation to the earliest demonstrated contract divergence.\\n3. Separate trigger, mechanism, contributing structural conditions, and correction category. Require causal justification for architectural change; retain proportionate local fixes when sufficient.\\n4. Support deterministic and probabilistic hypotheses, controlled experiments, uncertainty, and inconclusive outcomes without declaring a rerun a fix or requiring a flaky mechanism to fail every time.\\n5. Compose the correction handoff with `process-siren:improve-processes` when available, with a usable standalone contract when it is not installed.\\n6. Review tests for oracle independence, relevant fault sensitivity, behavior-preserving refactor tolerance, realistic boundaries, isolation, and diagnostic value. Preserve existing project gates rather than adding universal targets.\\n7. Add scenario-based evaluation fixtures and a baseline/candidate evaluation procedure; do not substitute keyword assertions for behavioral evaluation or claim unexecuted cases passed.\\n8. Keep corresponding Python entry points consistent and preserve standalone-plugin usability. Bump touched plugin manifests consistently.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Validation And Scope\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nValidate the changed artifacts using available tools, inspect the final diff, and record exact execution limitations. Independent fresh-agent evaluation and full repository CI are distinct from syntax or source review.\\n\\nThis is a process/skill correction, not a claim that the previously observed activation-matrix or other CI failures have been repaired. Do not modify production generators, regenerate the activation matrix to erase the failure, change CI gates, or merge as part of this task.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"51076a35f2d1dfa1ef2c6d0f5f582e769b28b1c3a65c88d17cb512c5856bb97d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXCLTzA\"}"}